1
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,710
Kirito...

2
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:17,680
Did you carry me all the way up here?

3
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:20,280
Damn right I did.

4
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:21,777
And it wasn't easy.

5
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:24,060
Maybe a thank you, or a...

6
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:25,940
What are you doing?

7
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:27,660
How disgusting!

8
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:29,737
You're completely drenched in sweat!

9
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:31,761
And you have stained my garments!

10
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:33,887
How dare you follow them up!

11
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:35,500
Are you kidding?

12
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:45,520
and I've opened my eyes I've made my eyes,

13
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:47,267
and I've made my path to you

14
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:03,440
I'm proud of myself Help! Help!

15
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:23,400
Where is your partner?

16
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:25,640
Hey, his name's Eugeo.

17
00:02:25,860 --> 00:02:27,400
Fine, Eugeo.

18
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:28,740
He is not here.

19
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:33,680
From the cloud-top garden,
there is a stairway leading up.

20
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:38,637
Before reaching this floor, however, he
would have had to face our strongest knight.

21
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:40,420
Yeah, and who would that be?

22
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:42,390
Uncle.

23
00:02:42,473 --> 00:02:44,240
Or rather, Commander Bercouli.

24
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:48,160
Oh man, now what?

25
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:54,937
I know.

26
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:56,137
System call.

27
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:57,740
Generate Umbra Element.

28
00:02:58,740 --> 00:02:59,799
Adhere Possession.

29
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:03,920
Object ID, WLSS-703.

30
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:05,550
Discharge.

31
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:07,687
What are you doing that for?

32
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:11,001
I'm trying to find where
the Blue Rose Sword's at.

33
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:13,640
If I can find it, I'm gonna find him.

34
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,940
He's under us.

35
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:20,460
One moment.

36
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:25,420
You did this, I take it? Yeah.

37
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:30,240
I managed to stop the bleeding, but
my sacred arts can only do so much.

38
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:34,688
Do you think you can
heal your eye yourself?

39
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:40,700
Not now.

40
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:43,688
There is not enough
sacred power in the air.

41
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:46,740
I cannot repair it until Solus has risen.

42
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:51,780
I am still feeling some pain, and
depth perception will be an issue.

43
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:54,514
But neither will keep me from fighting.

44
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:55,840
Are you sure?

45
00:03:56,540 --> 00:03:57,370
Yes.

46
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,100
I wish to feel this pain.

47
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:04,060
It is the proof of my
resolve to fight the church.

48
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:06,480
I am fine.

49
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:08,550
Okay.

50
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:15,660
I get it.

51
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:20,320
And if we're ever in battle, I'll
make sure to protect your right.

52
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:40,200
Is Yujiho the one responsible for this?

53
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:42,008
I'm pretty sure it was him.

54
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:46,566
I mean, remember how he activated
perfect control on us before?

55
00:04:46,740 --> 00:04:49,980
To be honest, I didn't
think it was this powerful.

56
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:53,300
It can't be. Uncle!

57
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:57,230
What the?

58
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:02,130
Uncle!

59
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:06,837
No way.

60
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,567
Eugeo didn't do that to him.

61
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:12,100
He did not, but I have an idea who did.

62
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:14,630
Years ago,

63
00:05:14,713 --> 00:05:17,797
Uncle told me that Prime
Senator Chudelkin had

64
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:20,880
been granted the authority
to turn anyone to stone.

65
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:23,360
An art called Deep Freeze.

66
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:24,790
Really?

67
00:05:24,873 --> 00:05:27,388
But they're supposed
to be on the same side.

68
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,717
Why would he betray
one of his own knights?

69
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:30,960
Doesn't make sense.

70
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:36,369
I think Uncle secretly harbored doubts
about the orders issued by the Senate.

71
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:37,840
And yet,

72
00:05:38,180 --> 00:05:39,010
like myself,

73
00:05:39,093 --> 00:05:43,637
he believed there could be no peace in
the realm without the rule of the Church.

74
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:46,820
So he continued to perform
his duties regardless.

75
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:55,197
The senator may have all
the authority, but this…

76
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:58,100
There is no reason to
treat him so horribly!

77
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:00,840
Son! Uncle!

78
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,510
Uncle!

79
00:06:10,593 --> 00:06:12,580
No, you mustn't try to move!

80
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:15,360
You'll destroy yourself! Stop it!

81
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,677
Hey, little girl.

82
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:24,080
Why don't you cut out that crying?

83
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:26,420
A smile suits you better.

84
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,190
Uncle!

85
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:30,490
Look at you.

86
00:06:30,573 --> 00:06:34,180
I guess you made it over that wall, kiddo.

87
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:37,320
For 300 years, I tried.

88
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:40,040
Couldn't break the seal. But you did.

89
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,780
What do I do?

90
00:06:42,020 --> 00:06:44,280
I can't just leave you here.

91
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:47,640
Don't you fuss over me.

92
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:49,840
I'm happy for you.

93
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:52,177
You're stronger than ever.

94
00:06:52,260 --> 00:06:54,820
There's nothing left for me to teach you.

95
00:06:54,980 --> 00:06:56,077
What are you saying?

96
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:57,300
That is not true.

97
00:06:57,640 --> 00:07:00,111
There is so much I need to learn from you.

98
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:02,740
You know all you need.

99
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:07,800
If anyone can guide this world to
where it ought to be, it's you.

100
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,937
Hey, punk.

101
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:15,280
Look after her for me.

102
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:17,440
You got it.

103
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:25,280
You want to find your partner,
Prime Senator Judelkin?

104
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:27,200
He took him.

105
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:31,640
Heading to the Pontifex's chamber.

106
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:38,680
However, hurry before the kid gets
trapped in the maze of his memories.

107
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:44,140
Thank you, Uncle.

108
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:54,060
No way.

109
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:16,237
some have tried to wield two
swords before mostly pretentious

110
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:20,297
upper-class noblemen looking to
impress you oddly enough seem

111
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:25,497
rather imposing oh you think I
can't imagine fighting with two

112
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:27,897
swords though that'd be crazy

113
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:34,377
all right by all accounts we must

114
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:39,197
assume the pontifex has eugeo by
now when she speaks one cannot

115
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:43,277
resist her words are a web which
entangle the mind like some kind

116
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:45,157
of hypnotist you talked to her

117
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:50,457
before only once it was six years

118
00:08:50,540 --> 00:08:54,920
ago i remember waking up and
the Pontifex standing before me.

119
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:59,580
She said she ruled the human empire
on behalf of the gods and had

120
00:09:00,220 --> 00:09:01,777
summoned me to serve their will.

121
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:05,260
Her eyes were like mirrors,
silver, and reflective.

122
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:09,000
I did not realize it at
the time, but I do now.

123
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:13,880
I was terrified of her, and
I knew I could not defy her.

124
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:18,860
I would accept every word she said
and serve her with all of my being.

125
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:21,057
The fear was absolute.

126
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:25,580
It compelled me to obey,
and like a coward, I did.

127
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:27,610
Alice.

128
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:32,220
Not to worry.

129
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:34,440
I know what I must do now.

130
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,626
For the sake of my sister
living in the North,

131
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:43,800
for my family and the citizens of this
realm, I will do what I believe is right.

132
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,360
We must hurry.

133
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:49,535
Time is short, and we still
have to reach the Pontifex.

134
00:09:50,140 --> 00:09:53,611
The Prime Senator will try to
stop us, so prepare yourself.

135
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:55,337
Wait, what about the commander?

136
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:57,126
We can't leave him like this.

137
00:09:57,960 --> 00:10:01,620
If we catch Chudelkin, we can
force him to reverse the spell.

138
00:10:02,180 --> 00:10:05,260
Or we can kill him and
solve the problem that way.

139
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:10,420
Hey. Yes?

140
00:10:11,020 --> 00:10:14,840
You mentioned this Prime Senator
Chudelkin guy a few times.

141
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:17,828
But what's the deal
with the other senators?

142
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:23,380
To be honest, none of us Integrity
Knights have ever seen the other Senators.

143
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:27,060
I know they are located
above the 96th floor.

144
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:30,032
We Knights are not allowed there, though.

145
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:32,002
You know what these Senators do?

146
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:34,060
They monitor the realm.

147
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:35,758
From their chamber,

148
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:38,717
they observe the words
and deeds of every citizen

149
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:42,100
to ensure they are not
violating the Taboo Index.

150
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:46,020
When someone runs afoul of the taboos,

151
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:50,280
they note the violation and
send a knight to deal with it.

152
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:54,520
So basically, they're pretty much
the eyes and ears of the Pontifex.

153
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:55,770
Although,

154
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:57,777
if Administrator's a control freak,

155
00:10:57,860 --> 00:11:01,331
it's hard to believe she'd give
anyone that much authority.

156
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:05,640
Is this where they are?

157
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:07,940
Yes, it should be.

158
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:19,740
That is a sacred art.

159
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:22,259
Doesn't sound like an attack spell.

160
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:25,120
Are you ready?

161
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:43,320
They're all just heads. Look again.

162
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:45,461
Their bodies seem to be attached.

163
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:57,777
that was a senator have
you seen one before

164
00:11:57,860 --> 00:12:01,740
yeah back at the academy
right after we fought

165
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:05,164
But Rios and Humber, he
appeared out of nowhere.

166
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:44,060
These miserable creatures
are the Senators?

167
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:46,240
What a horrifying fate.

168
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:48,120
Did the Pontifex do this?

169
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:49,920
Yeah, that's my bet.

170
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:51,925
These were once normal people.

171
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:54,595
Probably good at the sacred arts, too.

172
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:57,858
She kidnapped them and turned
them into these things.

173
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:00,630
Unforgivable.

174
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:04,490
No!

175
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:09,440
This will not - Who's that?

176
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:14,100
The Prime Senator...

177
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:15,930
Judelkin.

178
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,180
This cannot be happening!

179
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:27,660
This won't do! No, no, no!

180
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:29,720
It simply will not do!

181
00:13:31,740 --> 00:13:32,570
Oh!

182
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:49,820
If you attempt to initiate an art, I will
cut your tongue right out of your head.

183
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:51,600
That nerve!

184
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:53,780
Wait just a moment.

185
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:56,237
You should have died in
the fall with that traitor.

186
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:58,040
Why are you alive, Number 30?

187
00:13:58,340 --> 00:13:59,680
I am not a number.

188
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:03,197
My name is Alice.

189
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:05,480
I am no longer number 30.

190
00:14:08,140 --> 00:14:08,970
You!

191
00:14:09,053 --> 00:14:11,197
Why are you here? Number...

192
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,680
I mean Alice.

193
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:15,140
Why is your sword not embedded in him?

194
00:14:15,300 --> 00:14:16,418
Don't you remember?

195
00:14:16,580 --> 00:14:21,197
He's a heretic, a traitor, a pawn
of the Dark Territory! You're right.

196
00:14:21,280 --> 00:14:22,560
He is a traitor.

197
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:25,015
But he is not from the Dark Territory.

198
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:27,040
That I can assure you.

199
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:30,360
You miserable knight!

200
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:32,320
You wish to betray us too!

201
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:35,857
When I tell you to do
something, you damn well do it!

202
00:14:35,940 --> 00:14:37,517
You are nothing but a puppet!

203
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:38,960
All you knights are!

204
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:42,040
The Axiom Church turned us into puppets.

205
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:46,672
You sealed away our memories
through the Synthesis ritual,

206
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:50,080
forced us to be loyal
to you and the Church,

207
00:14:50,620 --> 00:14:54,900
made us believe the myth that we were
knights summoned from the heavens.

208
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:58,560
Yes, you are correct.

209
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:03,080
I remember the day we turned
you like it was yesterday.

210
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:09,140
You were so young, so innocent, so cute,
begging as tears streamed down your cheeks.

211
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:14,740
Please, don't take away my
memories of all the people I love!

212
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:16,215
Don't make me forget!

213
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:19,530
Why,

214
00:15:19,613 --> 00:15:20,977
just thinking about it again is going to

215
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:23,920
keep me awake all night
laughing hysterically.

216
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:25,877
As I recall,

217
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,237
you were brought here
from some backwater town

218
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:30,437
and trained as an
apprentice for two years.

219
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:32,677
You were so rebellious!

220
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:36,777
Once you snuck out to see the
Midsummer Festival like a tomboy.

221
00:15:36,860 --> 00:15:38,080
That said,

222
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:42,917
you studied hard, believing against all
hope that one day you'd return home again?

223
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,877
But you didn't.

224
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:46,260
And that's because,

225
00:15:46,740 --> 00:15:49,857
once you've raised your system
control authority level high enough?

226
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:52,177
It's forced synthesis time!

227
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:57,025
You should have seen your face when you
realized you'd never see your home again.

228
00:15:57,280 --> 00:16:00,197
I wanted to turn you to
stone so I could display

229
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:02,751
your precious grief in my chamber forever.

230
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:08,380
You mentioned something odd just now.

231
00:16:09,060 --> 00:16:10,220
Forced synthesis?

232
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:15,460
Do you mean to say the ritual can
be undertaken voluntarily as well?

233
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:18,200
My, my, what sharp ears you have.

234
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:19,909
You're absolutely correct.

235
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:24,300
Six years ago, you were
so unbelievably stubborn,

236
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:29,160
you refused to recite the secret commands
for the typical synthesis ritual.

237
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:33,233
Honestly, you were the most
insufferable brat imaginable.

238
00:16:33,620 --> 00:16:38,297
You gave me no choice but to divert the
automated senators from their normal duties,

239
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:43,321
then have them conduct a ritual to pry the
door open to your most precious memories.

240
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:46,400
It was a bother, but I shouldn't complain.

241
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:49,020
I got to see an incredible show!

242
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:53,240
He's talking way too much.

243
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:55,030
Yeah.

244
00:16:56,060 --> 00:16:57,760
Like he's stalling.

245
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:01,300
Prime Senator Chudelkin,

246
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:05,500
you had a lifetime of
amusement from my suffering.

247
00:17:05,860 --> 00:17:08,680
Now, at the end, I hope you are satisfied.

248
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:15,900
I have had enough of your dribble.

249
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:17,520
And you.

250
00:17:30,580 --> 00:17:31,880
You fools!

251
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:34,800
The ritual is not all I'm good at!

252
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:37,840
I will kill him.

253
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:39,620
Hey, wait up!

254
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:43,620
System call!

255
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:45,420
Generate humanist enemy!

256
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:47,517
Be on guard for a surprise attack.

257
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:48,480
You got it.

258
00:17:50,980 --> 00:17:53,420
He was chanting from here a moment ago.

259
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:57,280
The hundredth floor is above
us, so perhaps he fled there.

260
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:58,910
But how?

261
00:17:58,993 --> 00:18:01,260
I don't see stairs anywhere. Do you?

262
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:13,360
Great, another Integrity Knight.

263
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:15,180
No, that can't be.

264
